{"name":"Safe Haven","hex":"#5588aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safe haven","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place of safety or refuge.","A protected zone in a country, especially one designated for members of an ethnic or religious minority."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safe_haven"}],"entries":[{"title":"Safe Haven (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Safe Haven is a 2013 American romantic drama film starring Julianne Hough, Josh Duhamel and Cobie Smulders. The film marks the final film role for actor Red West. The film was directed by Lasse Hallström, and is an adaptation of Nicholas Sparks' 2010 novel. The film was originally set for a February 8 release. The film was released by Relativity Media on February 14, 2013 to negative reviews from critics and grossed $97.6 million against a $28 million budget."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3d/Safe_Haven_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safe_Haven_(film)"},{"title":"Safe Haven (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Safe Haven is the debut studio album by Canadian singer-songwriter Ruth B. Released on May 5, 2017, the album has been certified gold by Music Canada. Two of the songs from her debut extended play (EP), The Intro, are included in the album. Those are \"Lost Boy\" and \"Superficial Love\", though the production for \"Superficial Love\" is different from that of the EP. The album was produced by Joel Little, Mike Elizondo and Ruth Berhe."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d7/Safe_Haven_-_Ruth_B_album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safe_Haven_(album)"},{"title":"Sanctuary","blocks":[{"text":"A sanctuary, in its original meaning, is a sacred place, such as a shrine, protected by ecclesiastical immunity. By the use of such places as a haven, by extension the term has come to be used for any place of safety. This secondary use can be categorized into human sanctuary, a safe place for people, such as a political sanctuary; and non-human sanctuary, such as an animal or plant sanctuary."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/StMarysSanctuary.JPG/330px-StMarysSanctuary.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanctuary"},{"title":"Safe","blocks":[{"text":"A safe is a secure, lockable enclosure that protects objects against theft or fire. A safe is usually a hollow cuboid or cylinder, with one face being removable or hinged to form a door. The body and door may be cast from metal or formed out of plastic through blow molding. Bank teller safes are typically secured to the counter, have a slit opening for dropping valuables into the safe without opening it, and a time-delay combination lock to foil thieves. One key distinction between safe types is whether the safe is secured to a wall or structure or can be moved around."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Australian_Made_CMI_H2D_Home_Safe.JPG/330px-Australian_Made_CMI_H2D_Home_Safe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg/500px-Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg/1280px-Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg/500px-Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ajax the Younger violates Cassandra's sanctuary at the Palladium: tondo of an Attic cup, ca. 440–430 BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Sanctuary_marker_for_Holyrood_Abbey%2C_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh.jpg/500px-Sanctuary_marker_for_Holyrood_Abbey%2C_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Sanctuary_marker_for_Holyrood_Abbey%2C_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh.jpg/1280px-Sanctuary_marker_for_Holyrood_Abbey%2C_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Sanctuary_marker_for_Holyrood_Abbey%2C_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh.jpg/500px-Sanctuary_marker_for_Holyrood_Abbey%2C_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sanctuary marker (S) at Holyrood Abbey, Royal Mile, Edinburgh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASanctuary_marker_for_Holyrood_Abbey%2C_Royal_Mile%2C_Edinburgh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Link%C3%B6pings_domkyrka%2C_koret.jpg/120px-Link%C3%B6pings_domkyrka%2C_koret.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Link%C3%B6pings_domkyrka%2C_koret.jpg/250px-Link%C3%B6pings_domkyrka%2C_koret.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Link%C3%B6pings_domkyrka%2C_koret.jpg/120px-Link%C3%B6pings_domkyrka%2C_koret.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALink%C3%B6pings_domkyrka%2C_koret.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/V%C3